# 118 (found 2026-10-07 covering the G12 phase 12 spread meet): a
# template met again through a disjunction, beside a count, with more
# than one term the other arm's template lacks, never settles in
# TypeScript. Go generates the data, and so do both ports with one new
# term or without the count.
#
# expected: {"x":["a",1,true]}, in both ports
# actual:   [aontu/unify_cycle] at $.x.0 (TypeScript only; `empty` before
#           the fix of BUGS.md 110)
%t = match(key(0), "1", number, any) & match(key(0), "2", boolean, any)
x: (map|[&: match(key(0), "0", string, any)]) & (map|[&: %t] & len(max(5)))
x: ["a", 1, true]
